            <ArticleTitle>Immunotherapy: new guidelines suggest a 'window' for prevention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-61, 50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>New guidelines suggest that immunotherapy can, in some cases, actually prevent the development of allergic asthma in children with allergic rhinitis. The new recommendations offer advice on when to consider immunotherapy, optimal dosing, and how to handle and store medicines.</AbstractText>
